module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Codimension.AffineOpenHeight
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Fibres.BertiniChartEquation

/-!
# The common zero locus of a linear system and its trace on a trivializing chart

In the standing situation of the Bertini theorems ([Stacks, Tag 0G47]) every vector `v` of the
linear system `V` cuts out a divisor `H_v = Z(ψ(v))` on `X`, and the hypotheses of
[Stacks, Tag 0G4F] are conditions on these divisors and on the *common zero locus*

`Z = ⋂_{v ∈ V} H_v`.

This module provides the vocabulary — `divisor`, `divisorSet`, `commonZeroSet` — and the one
computation that turns a condition on `Z` into a condition on the ring of a trivializing affine
open `U = Spec A` of `X`: the trace of `H_w` on `U` is the zero locus of the function `f_w ∈ A`
representing `ψ(w)` under a trivialization of `L` over `U`, and `f_w` lies in the ideal
`(f₁, …, f_r)` generated by the functions representing the basis vectors. Consequently the zero
locus of `(f₁, …, f_r)` in `Spec A` lands inside `Z`, which is what lets hypothesis (4) of the
tag be read as a height bound on the minimal primes of `(f₁, …, f_r)`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.le_height_of_mem_minimalPrimes_of_isAffineOpen`).

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.divisor` is `H_w = Z(ψ(w))`, as a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf on
  `X`, and `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.divisorSet` is its support.
* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.commonZeroSet` is `Z = ⋂_{v ∈ V} H_v`.
* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.chartFunction` is the function `f_w ∈ Γ(U, ⊤)` representing
  `ψ(w)` under a trivialization of `L` over `U`; on a basis vector it is
  `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.chartEquation`.
* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.chartFrameSections` is a trivialization read on global
  sections, `Γ(L|_U, ⊤) ≃ₗ Γ(U, ⊤)`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.ideal_divisor_comap_ι`: the ideal of `H_w` on a trivializing
  affine open is generated by `f_w`.
* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.mem_divisorSet_iff`: a point of `U` lies in `|H_w|` exactly
  when `f_w` vanishes at it.
* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.chartFunction_mem_span_image`: `w ↦ f_w` is semilinear over
  `k → Γ(U, ⊤)`, so a vector in the `k`-span of a set `s` of vectors has its function in the
  ideal of `Γ(U, ⊤)` generated by the functions of `s`.
* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.chartFunction_mem_span_chartEquation`: `f_w` lies in the ideal
  generated by `f₁, …, f_r`, because `w` is a linear combination of the basis vectors. This is
  the case `s = {v₁, …, v_r}` of the previous one.
* `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.image_zeroLocus_subset_commonZeroSet`: the zero locus of
  `(f₁, …, f_r)` on the chart lands in `Z`. This is the inclusion `⋂ᵢ H_{vᵢ} ⊆ ⋂_{v ∈ V} H_v`,
  read on a chart; the reverse inclusion is trivial.

## Implementation notes

The trace is computed by pulling the ideal sheaf back along the open immersion `U → X` rather
than by evaluating it on the affine open `U` of `X`: the pullback lives on `U.toScheme`, whose
ring of global sections `Γ(U.toScheme, ⊤)` is the ring in which `chartEquation` already lives,
so no transport along `Scheme.Opens.topIso` is needed. The two ingredients are
`Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme_pullback` ([Stacks, Tag 0B6Y]), which says the pullback of a zero
scheme is the zero scheme of the pulled-back section, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme_ideal_of_trivialization` ([Stacks, Tag 02OQ]), which reads the
ideal off a trivialization.

The linearity of `w ↦ f_w` is semilinear over `k → Γ(U, ⊤)`: a scalar of `k` acts on the global
sections of `L` through the structure morphism (`Stacks.Bertini.baseRingHom`), and pulling back
to `U` composes that with `U.ι`. Only the consequence
`chartFunction_mem_span_chartEquation` is needed, so the semilinear structure is not packaged.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G47](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G47)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0G4F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0G4F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OQ)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite

universe u v

namespace Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors

variable (D : FamilyDivisors.{u, v})

/-! ### The divisors of the linear system and their common zero locus -/

/-- **The divisor `H_w = Z(ψ(w))`** cut out on `X` by a vector of the linear system, as a
quasi-coherent ideal sheaf. -/
@[stacks 0G47 "the divisor of a vector of the linear system"]
def divisor (w : D.V) : D.X.IdealSheafData :=
  zeroScheme D.X D.L (D.sectionOf w)

/-- The support `|H_w| ⊆ X` of the divisor of a vector of the linear system. -/
def divisorSet (w : D.V) : Set D.X := (D.divisor w).supportSet

/-- The support `|H_w|` of the divisor of a vector is closed in `X`. -/
theorem isClosed_divisorSet (w : D.V) : IsClosed (D.divisorSet w) :=
  Scheme.IdealSheafData.isClosed_supportSet _

/-- **The common zero locus `Z = ⋂_{v ∈ V} H_v`** of the linear system. This is the closed set
on which hypothesis (4) of [Stacks, Tag 0G4F] imposes a codimension bound. -/
@[stacks 0G4F "the common zero locus of the linear system"]
def commonZeroSet : Set D.X := ⋂ w : D.V, D.divisorSet w

/-- The common zero locus `Z` of the linear system is closed in `X`. -/
theorem isClosed_commonZeroSet : IsClosed D.commonZeroSet :=
  isClosed_iInter fun w => D.isClosed_divisorSet w

/-- The common zero locus `Z` is contained in the support of every divisor `H_w`. -/
theorem commonZeroSet_subset_divisorSet (w : D.V) : D.commonZeroSet ⊆ D.divisorSet w :=
  Set.iInter_subset _ w

/-! ### The sections of the basis span -/

/-- The scalar of `Γ(X, ⊤)` through which a scalar of `k` acts on the global sections of `L`:
its image under the structure morphism on global sections. -/
def baseScalar (c : D.k) : Γ(D.X, ⊤) :=
  baseRingHom D.k D.toBase c

/-- The `k`-action on the sections of `L` is the action of `Γ(X, ⊤)` through the structure
morphism. -/
theorem sectionOf_smul (c : D.k) (w : D.V) :
    D.sectionOf (c • w) = D.baseScalar c • D.sectionOf w :=
  D.ψ.map_smul c w

/-- The section of a sum of vectors is the sum of their sections. -/
theorem sectionOf_add (w w' : D.V) :
    D.sectionOf (w + w') = D.sectionOf w + D.sectionOf w' :=
  D.ψ.map_add w w'

/-- The section of the zero vector is zero. -/
theorem sectionOf_zero : D.sectionOf (0 : D.V) = 0 :=
  D.ψ.map_zero

/-- The section of a vector is the corresponding combination of the sections of the basis. -/
theorem sectionOf_eq_sum (w : D.V) :
    D.sectionOf w = ∑ i, D.baseScalar (D.basis.repr w i) • D.sectionOf (D.basis i) := by
  classical
  conv_lhs => rw [← D.basis.sum_repr w]
  show D.ψ (∑ i, D.basis.repr w i • D.basis i) = _
  rw [map_sum]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => D.sectionOf_smul _ _

/-! ### The trace of a divisor on a trivializing affine chart -/

section Chart

variable {D} {U : D.X.Opens}
  (eU : D.restrictedModule U ≅ SheafOfModules.unit U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)

/-- **A trivialization of `L` over `U`, read on global sections.** -/
def chartFrameSections :
    Γ(D.restrictedModule U, ⊤) ≃ₗ[Γ(U.toScheme, ⊤)] Γ(U.toScheme, ⊤) :=
  haveI : IsIso (Scheme.Modules.Hom.app eU.hom ⊤) :=
    Scheme.Modules.Hom.isIso_iff_isIso_app.mp eU.isIso_hom ⊤
  LinearEquiv.ofBijective
    ({ toFun := fun t => eU.hom.app ⊤ t
       map_add' := fun a b => map_add _ a b
       map_smul' := fun r t => Scheme.Modules.Hom.app_smul eU.hom r t } :
      Γ(D.restrictedModule U, ⊤) →ₗ[Γ(U.toScheme, ⊤)] Γ(U.toScheme, ⊤))
    (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso (eU.hom.app ⊤))

/-- The trivialization on global sections is the component of `eU` on `⊤`. -/
@[simp]
theorem chartFrameSections_apply (t : Γ(D.restrictedModule U, ⊤)) :
    chartFrameSections eU t = eU.hom.app ⊤ t := rfl

/-- **The function representing `ψ(w)` on a trivializing open.** On a basis vector this is
`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.chartEquation`. -/
def chartFunction (w : D.V) : Γ(U.toScheme, ⊤) :=
  chartFrameSections eU (D.restrictedSection U w)

/-- The function of the basis vector `vᵢ` is `chartEquation eU i`. -/
theorem chartFunction_basis (i : Fin (Module.finrank D.k D.V)) :
    chartFunction eU (D.basis i) = D.chartEquation eU i :=
  rfl

/-- **The ideal of `H_w` on a trivializing affine chart is generated by `f_w`.** -/
theorem ideal_divisor_comap_ι [IsAffine U.toScheme] (w : D.V) :
    ((D.divisor w).comap U.ι).ideal ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top U.toScheme⟩ =
      Ideal.span {chartFunction eU w} := by
  let := D.isInvertible
  have hpull : (D.divisor w).comap U.ι =
      zeroScheme U.toScheme (D.restrictedModule U) (D.restrictedSection U w) :=
    (Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme_pullback U.ι D.L (D.sectionOf w)).symm
  rw [hpull]
  refine AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme_ideal_of_trivialization U.toScheme
    (D.restrictedModule U) (D.restrictedSection U w) ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top U.toScheme⟩
    (chartFrameSections eU) (chartFunction eU w) ?_
  have hid : (D.restrictedModule U).presheaf.map
      (homOfLE (le_top : (⊤ : U.toScheme.Opens) ≤ ⊤)).op (D.restrictedSection U w) =
      D.restrictedSection U w := by simp
  rw [hid]
  rfl

/-- **A point of a trivializing affine chart lies in `|H_w|` exactly when `f_w` vanishes
there.** -/
theorem mem_divisorSet_iff [IsAffine U.toScheme] (w : D.V) (x : U.toScheme) :
    U.ι.base x ∈ D.divisorSet w ↔
      x ∈ U.toScheme.zeroLocus (U := ⊤) {chartFunction eU w} := by
  have hmem : x ∈ ((D.divisor w).comap U.ι).supportSet ↔
      U.ι.base x ∈ (D.divisor w).supportSet := by
    rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_supportSet_iff_mem_support,
      Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_supportSet_iff_mem_support,
      Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap]
    exact Iff.rfl
  rw [divisorSet, ← hmem,
    Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_supportSet_iff_of_mem
      (U := ⟨⊤, isAffineOpen_top U.toScheme⟩) (by trivial),
    ideal_divisor_comap_ι eU w, Scheme.zeroLocus_span]

end Chart

/-! ### The chart functions of the basis generate -/

section Span

variable {D} {U : D.X.Opens}
  (eU : D.restrictedModule U ≅ SheafOfModules.unit U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf)

/-- The restricted section of a vector is the corresponding combination of the restricted
sections of the basis, with coefficients pulled back to `U`. -/
theorem restrictedSection_eq_sum (w : D.V) :
    D.restrictedSection U w =
      ∑ i, U.ι.appTop (D.baseScalar (D.basis.repr w i)) • D.restrictedSection U (D.basis i) := by
  classical
  show pullbackGlobalSections U.ι D.L (D.sectionOf w) = _
  rw [D.sectionOf_eq_sum w, map_sum]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ =>
    SectionsEqualizer.pullbackGlobalSections_smul U.ι D.L _ _

/-! ### Semilinearity of the chart function -/

/-- The chart function of a vector, unfolded to the frame applied to the pulled-back section. -/
private theorem chartFunction_eq (w : D.V) :
    chartFunction eU w =
      chartFrameSections eU (pullbackGlobalSections U.ι D.L (D.sectionOf w)) :=
  rfl

/-- The function of the zero vector is zero. -/
@[simp]
theorem chartFunction_zero : chartFunction eU (0 : D.V) = 0 := by
  rw [chartFunction_eq, D.sectionOf_zero, map_zero, map_zero]

/-- The function of a sum of vectors is the sum of their functions. -/
theorem chartFunction_add (w w' : D.V) :
    chartFunction eU (w + w') = chartFunction eU w + chartFunction eU w' := by
  simp only [chartFunction_eq, D.sectionOf_add, map_add]

/-- **The function of a scalar multiple.** The scalar acts through the structure morphism of `X`
restricted to `U`. -/
theorem chartFunction_smul (a : D.k) (w : D.V) :
    chartFunction eU (a • w) = U.ι.appTop (D.baseScalar a) * chartFunction eU w := by
  rw [chartFunction_eq, chartFunction_eq, D.sectionOf_smul a w,
    SectionsEqualizer.pullbackGlobalSections_smul, map_smul, smul_eq_mul]

/-- **The function of a vector of a subspace lies in the ideal generated by the functions of a
spanning set of that subspace.** If `w` lies in the `k`-span of `s`, then `f_w` lies in the ideal
of `Γ(U, ⊤)` generated by the `f_v` for `v ∈ s`. -/
theorem chartFunction_mem_span_image {s : Set D.V} {w : D.V} (hw : w ∈ Submodule.span D.k s) :
    chartFunction eU w ∈ Ideal.span (chartFunction eU '' s) := by
  induction hw using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem x hx => exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  | zero => simp
  | add x y _ _ hx hy => rw [chartFunction_add]; exact Ideal.add_mem _ hx hy
  | smul a x _ hx => rw [chartFunction_smul]; exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ hx

/-- **The function of any vector lies in the ideal generated by the functions of the basis.**
A vector `w` of the linear system is a `k`-linear combination of the basis vectors, and
`w ↦ f_w` is semilinear over `k → Γ(U, ⊤)`, so `f_w ∈ (f₁, …, f_r)`. -/
theorem chartFunction_mem_span_chartEquation (w : D.V) :
    chartFunction eU w ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range (D.chartEquation eU)) := by
  have himg : chartFunction eU '' Set.range D.basis = Set.range (D.chartEquation eU) := by
    rw [← Set.range_comp]
    rfl
  rw [← himg]
  exact chartFunction_mem_span_image eU (by rw [D.basis.span_eq]; exact Submodule.mem_top)

/-- **The zero locus of the basis functions on a chart lands in the common zero locus.** A point
of the chart at which every `fᵢ` vanishes lies in `H_w` for *every* vector `w` of the linear
system, not only for the basis vectors: this is the inclusion `⋂ᵢ H_{vᵢ} ⊆ ⋂_{v ∈ V} H_v`. -/
theorem image_zeroLocus_subset_commonZeroSet [IsAffine U.toScheme] :
    U.ι.base '' U.toScheme.zeroLocus (U := ⊤)
        ((Ideal.span (Set.range (D.chartEquation eU)) : Ideal Γ(U.toScheme, ⊤)) :
          Set Γ(U.toScheme, ⊤)) ⊆ D.commonZeroSet := by
  rintro _ ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
  refine Set.mem_iInter.mpr fun w => ?_
  rw [mem_divisorSet_iff eU w x, Scheme.mem_zeroLocus_iff]
  rintro f (rfl : f = chartFunction eU w)
  exact (U.toScheme.mem_zeroLocus_iff _ x).mp hx _ (chartFunction_mem_span_chartEquation eU w)

end Span

end Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors

end
